---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<LegalPage accent="Terms" title="Terms of Use" description={`Terms for using the ${site.name} template catalog, including the referral link disclosure.`} updated="November 3, 2026">
  <p>
    By using this site you agree to these terms. {site.name} is a catalog that presents templates made by {site.name}. This site does not take payments.
  </p>

  <h2>Buying and using templates</h2>
  <p>
    Framer templates are previewed, bought and remixed on <a href="https://www.framer.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Framer</a>.{' '}
    Purchases, payments, refunds and licenses are handled by Framer under its own terms and the license shown on each
    template's Framer page.
  </p>
  <p>
    A few Framer templates are sold directly through <a href="https://contra.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Contra</a> instead. The template page says where.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some templates also have a code version, sold through <a href="https://contra.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Contra</a>.{' '}
    Contra handles the payment. The files follow the <a href="/license/">code license</a> and the <a href="/refunds/">refund policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Referral links</h2>
  <p>
    Some links to Framer on this site are referral links. If you sign up for or upgrade a Framer plan after following
    one, {site.name} may earn a commission. It costs you nothing extra and does not change which templates we show.
  </p>

  <h2>Content</h2>
  <p>
    Template names, previews, descriptions and the site design belong to {site.name}. Please don't copy them without
    permission. Prices, features and availability are shown in good faith; the Framer page is the final word.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    The site is provided as is. We are not responsible for third-party sites we link to, and to the extent the law
    allows, we are not liable for any loss arising from using this site.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms. The current version is always on this page.</p>
</LegalPage>
